divergence_reason = sanctioned: this program exercises the full `Std.Db.Sql` combinator family (backlog #61: column, param, int, string, float, bool, eq, ne, gt, lt, gte, lte, and, or, not, isNull, isNotNull, inList, like) plus Db.findWhere — none of these have a Go counterpart (ipê-only addition, no Go reference exists to diverge from). The Go backend and ipê otherwise share the Sky stdlib surface but emit different SQLite drivers (Go+cgo vs Rust+sqlx) with different in-memory connection-pool behaviour, so even the shared subset of this program (Db.open/withTransaction/exec) would not run identically on both backends. ipê's output is recorded as the correct reference.
